Dear all,

I am working with a hedgehog search-based SCR dataset collected from 2009 - 2022. Preliminary results (with D~session) showed that the population density is basically stable across year sessions.

But the population had a gradual spatial shifting from south to north. In the middle of the study, a group of intro-guild predators joined in south, and probably due to this, the population gradually shifted to north where there were more hedgerows and bushes which could work as shelters. Single session modeling density as a function of scaled distance to hedgerows (D ~ d2hedge) basically reflected this effect, i.e., the coefficient values of d2hedge gradually increased. I tried to incorporate this year interactive effect into multiple session modeling with the below code. With just two years, it worked but for some parameters the result is quite different with that from single session modeling ( each year modeled separately). So, could anyone please help me to check if my below code makes sense or totally not?

oSCR.fit(model = list(D~ session + d2hedge + grass + session:d2hedge + session:d2grass, p0~habitattype+sex, sig~sex, asu~ d2alledge),  scrFrame= hog.sf, ssDF = hog.ssDF, costDF = hog.cs, distmet = "ecol")

Another question is about the plotting.
The density surface is nicely produced with:
     density <- predict.oSCR(model1, hog.sf, hog.ssDF, override.trim=TRUE)
      plot(density$r[[1]])

But for connectivity surface (I have already got the a2 value), I am struggling to find where are the detailed connectivity values? Anyone please could you let me know where to find the detailed connectivity output so I can get it plotted?

Thank you very much in advance!

Best regards,
Hongli

